{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0c3d655cc8da39df988898bf2762492a5a7366ac063243388f8af8622853351c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Header comment syntax adapts to the language: PHP/TS/Go use //, Python uses docstrings, Ruby uses #, and Blade uses {{-- --}}."},{"claim_ids":["clm_46020c87fe9e583359f2f757c200b53ff09d372ed450381b9b2d70410d2123e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The docs state these are historical results whose raw run artifacts are not included in the checkout, so CI does not claim to reproduce the numerical advantage; versioned traces and a reproduction command are required first."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6d5dbae82c73711ab5230e04e374ac3d97233304aff66398d5f5a2867f2f7d5a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"codedna install creates a .codedna directory, installs a Git pre-commit gate, and adds the selected agent's instruction file while preserving existing instruction files and hooks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8f04bee140652d5709f0620afb3e0aa6e6dd82eed9715c3ab9084056ad4746ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI is installed via pipx and requires Python 3.11+; non-Python language adapters rely on tree-sitter, while Swift and VB.NET use structural parsers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9ac30038584937f8777a79e6bdfbf103fcd8c526b53aa592e586896916ed5d3e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Python is described as the most tested language; non-Python adapters have seen less real-world usage, and users are asked to report wrong exports or header format issues."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d40d4d6f8200614834eb2f1e31aefeb44a2cfa513adc2151e211443db498edc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The protocol embeds structured header fields in source files: exports, used_by (importers, with [cascade] markers), related (semantic links without imports), rules, wiki pointers, and agent messages with model and date."},{"claim_ids":["clm_abd15c7722d159cbbdb92933104dd0a95eea5618208fcabd6db94924474f1f65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a CLI with commands including init, update, refresh, check, verify, impact, doctor, manifest, mode, install, and wiki bootstrap/sync, all of which auto-detect languages."},{"claim_ids":["clm_af1c9de4d49fbf9c5348cf643f93d97bc44563485a9aed5a90cb827ff5bf346a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An optional post-commit wiki-sync hook regenerates docs/codedna-wiki.md after each commit; it is non-blocking (failures silenced) and never overwrites an existing hook, looking for a CodeDNA marker instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c959748cf46bb5ab3531ea2a4dcb6b933f5bc57f113433b0f7e3fb67950407be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Claude Code plugin exposes slash commands (/codedna:init, /codedna:check, /codedna:manifest, /codedna:impact) as an alternative to the CLI for Claude Code users."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc13f5b7ffcb9ed5fb15c552d81feb0bf2f192f6df1dc5d41b6039f454f3de71"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"codedna install supports a --tools flag selecting integrations for agents such as claude, codex, opencode, aider, cursor, copilot, cline, windsurf, roo, and agents, writing the corresponding instruction files and hooks."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0c3d655cc8da39df988898bf2762492a5a7366ac063243388f8af8622853351c","clm_46020c87fe9e583359f2f757c200b53ff09d372ed450381b9b2d70410d2123e4","clm_6d5dbae82c73711ab5230e04e374ac3d97233304aff66398d5f5a2867f2f7d5a","clm_8f04bee140652d5709f0620afb3e0aa6e6dd82eed9715c3ab9084056ad4746ef","clm_9ac30038584937f8777a79e6bdfbf103fcd8c526b53aa592e586896916ed5d3e","clm_9d40d4d6f8200614834eb2f1e31aefeb44a2cfa513adc2151e211443db498edc","clm_abd15c7722d159cbbdb92933104dd0a95eea5618208fcabd6db94924474f1f65","clm_af1c9de4d49fbf9c5348cf643f93d97bc44563485a9aed5a90cb827ff5bf346a","clm_c959748cf46bb5ab3531ea2a4dcb6b933f5bc57f113433b0f7e3fb67950407be","clm_fc13f5b7ffcb9ed5fb15c552d81feb0bf2f192f6df1dc5d41b6039f454f3de71"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_574784064c92466190c61ed79f9c4459","id":"pg_4753b9e158e35f6683c5aaf46db6448c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/larens94-codedna-readme-md-b3fe577b47c9-aaf46db6448c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_894a3453ecb25793b2490f76a7f4712a"],"title":"Larens94/codedna/README.md @ b3fe577b47c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_574784064c92466190c61ed79f9c4459"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_46020c87fe9e583359f2f757c200b53ff09d372ed450381b9b2d70410d2123e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The docs state these are historical results whose raw run artifacts are not included in the checkout, so CI does not claim to reproduce the numerical advantage; versioned traces and a reproduction command are required first."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85c91b3ba0efda61cb94dea0fe86ae9bc7fe9e01c8ce45932bf18c018ebf9040"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The benchmark notes CodeDNA v0.7 shows roughly zero benefit on cross-cutting tasks with no call chain (e.g. task 11808); a proposed cross_cutting_patterns: feature is referenced in SPEC.md §2.4, and the related: field addresses the cross-cutting gap."}],"claim_ids":["clm_46020c87fe9e583359f2f757c200b53ff09d372ed450381b9b2d70410d2123e4","clm_85c91b3ba0efda61cb94dea0fe86ae9bc7fe9e01c8ce45932bf18c018ebf9040"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_574784064c92466190c61ed79f9c4459","id":"pg_724ec84b5fae561d8461e484abf8be2b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/larens94-codedna-docs-benchmark-md-b3fe577b47c9-e484abf8be2b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_36d95e3ec7005e6389ad5bbfe69f485f"],"title":"Larens94/codedna/docs/benchmark.md @ b3fe577b47c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_574784064c92466190c61ed79f9c4459"}
